      "content": "uh, i'm not sure what you mean by the goblin stuff, can we just stick to the logistics? \n\nregarding the \"small, unnoticed error\" you mentioned, i've already checked the logs and the physical counts seem solid. we've even done a double count on the SN-112-Q because the variance was higher there. could you give me a more technical list of potential causes for this kind of shrinkage? like, what are the standard operational reasons for recurring small variances in high-density electronic storage?",
